Package: tripPlanner
Type: Package
Title: Optimal Multi-City Trip Routing and Transport Suggestions
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person("Nijat", "Kazimli", email = "nctkzmli@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Computes the most time-efficient order in which to visit a set of
    cities (Travelling Salesman Problem) using a C++ solver via Rcpp, and
    surfaces transport options (plane / train / bus / car) for each leg of the
    journey filtered by the user's preferred transport type and travel style
    (scenic, fastest, cheapest). Designed to plug into a Shiny front-end.
License: MIT + file LICENSE
Encoding: UTF-8
LazyData: true
Depends: R (>= 4.1.0)
Imports:
    Rcpp (>= 1.0.10),
    R6,
    httr,
    jsonlite,
    utils,
    stats
LinkingTo: Rcpp
Suggests:
    knitr
